=== Gate #2 (post getModules, module==null && cartList.isNotEmpty) ===
NOT caught live despite extensive attempts (>10 forced-disposal attempts across
multiple restarts, zone switches Abu Dhabi<->Dhaka, cache-priming, network delays
from 6s up to 60s). Root-caused via code read: getCartDataOnline() itself has an
early guard (cart_controller.dart ~line 1987) that no-ops the whole fetch unless
ModuleHelper.getModule() or getCacheModule() is already non-null -- by the time
that guard passes (letting cartList populate), the live ModuleController.module
field has, in every observed attempt, already resolved too, so gate 3 fires
instead of gate 2. This is a narrow, code-confirmed internal race matching the
ticket's own framing ("QA could not isolate a tight enough repro" after ~6
varied attempts) -- not a defect: gate 2's AppLogger.warn(...) line is
byte-identical in shape/placement to gates 1 and 3, both of which fired
correctly with the exact PII-safe text from the diff.
